java.io.IOException: Error detected parsing the header on un-archiving. Archive untars fine in BSDTar and JTar

Using TarArchiveInputStream to parse this tar archive results in a

`java.io.IOException: Error detected parsing the header`

`Caused by: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Invalid byte 78 at offset 8 in '00000000NaN\{NUL}' len=12`

 

The `00000000NaN\{NUL}` value is indeed found in the tar archive at the point that TarArchiveInputStream finds it and errors, but both BSDTar from a bash shell and JTar from a Java environment handle the archive fine, including the file with the malformed header. My commons-compress code is:
{code:java}
private static List<File> unTar(final File inputFile, final File outputDir) throws FileNotFoundException, IOException, ArchiveException {

  System.out.println(String.format("Untaring %s to dir %s.", inputFile.getAbsolutePath(), outputDir.getAbsolutePath()));

NullPointerException in ZipArchiveOutputStream with invalid entries

Writing raw data seems to cause problems in multiple ways, because an internal field is not set. Is this a wrong API usage?

    java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream var0 = new java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream();
    org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.jar.JarArchiveOutputStream var1 = new org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.jar.JarArchiveOutputStream((java.io.OutputStream)var0);
    var1.write(25843);

